  "body": "Following up from https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/3745#issuecomment-487192709, the [`autocomplete=one-time-code`](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-control-infrastructure.html#attr-fe-autocomplete-one-time-code) specification doesn't tell a website author enough to know how they should send an SMS that'll actually autofill on the user's platform. Do they need to user-agent-sniff to get the right format on iOS vs Android? Is @mikewest right in https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/3745#issuecomment-395327173 that browsers on Android can't auto-fill this at all?",
